  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "At Capri Palace, Tonino Cacace made contemporary art part of the experience of staying in a hotel. His collection brought works by Giorgio de Chirico, Mimmo Paladino and Fabrizio Plessi into its rooms and public spaces. Paintings, sculpture and installations gave the property a cultural identity beyond its accommodation.\n\nIn Tuscany, Cacace acquired L’Olmo near Pienza in 2014 and developed a different setting for hospitality. He and Sara Iannuzzi worked with architect Fabrizia Frezza’s studio on the restoration of a seventeenth-century farmhouse. Original architectural features remained central to the design: a former granary became a suite, while its pierced brick wall retained views across the countryside.",
